WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.252
Hey what's up guys, I'm Tony Gonzalez, I'm here with Bleacher Report,

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:03.837
and this is: Build Your Squad.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.176
All right, I'm gonna pick my all-time NFL squad.

00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:14.222
Well, you always gotta start with a quarterback, so I'm going to start with...

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.307
Joe Montana.

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:22.230
My guy. I grew up in L.A. watching all those great 49er teams back in the '80s.

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:24.024
And then playing for the Kansas City Chiefs

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:26.026
where he played for the last couple years of his career,

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:27.235
I loved him.

00:00:27.235 --> 00:00:30.196
Threw a perfect ball, nice little spiral, looked very catchable.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:33.867
And you want that as a guy who catches the ball, so I gotta go with him.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.785
Then from there we'll go with...

00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:36.745
the running backs.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.831
I'm gonna take Barry Sanders.

00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:43.168
Loved watching him. I was a Tecmo Bowl guy too,

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:45.336
and when you had Barry Sanders playing Tecmo Bowl,

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.297
you couldn't be tackled. He was the guy.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.381
Just couldn't tackle him.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:52.218
And he's, he's so little, he's a little guy, and they couldn't get a hold of him,

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.262
so I loved watching him play.

00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:55.221
Uhh...

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.681
wide...

00:00:57.474 --> 00:00:57.891
oh I'mma,

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:58.641
I'mma,

00:00:58.850 --> 00:00:59.642
I'mma go with him.

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:00.602
I'mma go with Tony Gonzalez

00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:03.521
because I think it would be silly not to pick myself.

00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:05.774
And I owe it to myself, ya know?

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:07.609
And I'm proud of myself,

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:08.568
I'm not gonna lie.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.112
And, uh, I was pretty good for a while.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.157
I'm gonna go Lawrence Taylor, come on.

00:01:14.532 --> 00:01:15.533
Lawrence Taylor,

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:18.661
"Let's go out there like a bunch of crazed dogs and have some fun!"

00:01:18.661 --> 00:01:20.789
I don't know if you remember him saying that, but

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:22.082
Lawrence Taylor said it. I didn't say that.

00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:23.625
That guy was the man.

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:27.087
Sacks, against the run, everything else, and then...

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:28.755
after that...

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:29.798
I'm taking...

00:01:30.173 --> 00:01:30.840
Reggie White.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:33.760
The most dominant defensive player

00:01:34.177 --> 00:01:37.305
I've ever seen. I had a chance to actually play against him towards the end of his career.

00:01:37.555 --> 00:01:40.892
But just a guy—in the locker room too, you need somebody in the locker room

00:01:40.892 --> 00:01:42.977
to get everybody's spirit right before the game,

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:47.565
but then go out there like a madman and terrorize opponents.

00:01:47.565 --> 00:01:49.484
So that's a good squad right there.

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:52.112
I think we can beat anybody. I'd love to see everybody else's squad,

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.279
cuz I think that beats everybody.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.614
What's missing from this team is,

00:01:55.156 --> 00:01:56.157
well, you need a wide receiver.

00:01:56.157 --> 00:01:58.493
Cuz I don't wanna be just the main guy and—

00:01:58.493 --> 00:02:00.995
I'm fast but I'm not that fast. I need somebody to get over the top...

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:04.040
so if I'm adding a guy, it's gonna be um...

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.628
I'll probably, I'mma go with Randy.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:13.842
Randy Moss, the one-handed catches, the freak speed,

00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:17.679
just a 4.2 guy—I don't know how fast he was but—

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:21.141
jumping up over everybody with this guy throwing the ball, Joe Montana,

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.601
to Randy Moss, it can't be beat.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.812
If you got him going over the top, me working the middle

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.814
and Barry Sanders out of the backfield, you can't stop that.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:31.526
These two, I don't care who you are, you're not blocking these two guys, so,

00:02:31.526 --> 00:02:32.152
lock picks.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:33.820
Lock 'em in.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:38.575
So this is my squad. Obviously Joe Montana, to me, the greatest of all time.

00:02:38.575 --> 00:02:39.909
Barry Sanders out of the backfield.

00:02:40.702 --> 00:02:42.912
Me at tight end, working the middle of the field.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:44.330
Red zone.

00:02:44.539 --> 00:02:46.833
He's not on here, but Randy Moss would be over the top.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.627
He'd be the guy to put the speed, take the top off the defense.

00:02:49.794 --> 00:02:50.795
But then on defense,

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.381
my man, Lawrence Taylor. L.T. coming off the edge.

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:55.508
And then Reggie White working the middle...

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.801
actually he can come off the edge too.

00:02:56.926 --> 00:02:59.637
Imagine those guys coming off the edge, collapsing that pocket.

00:03:00.972 --> 00:03:01.973
A quarterback's got no shot, so

00:03:02.807 --> 00:03:04.934
this squad right here, I'm pretty, pretty proud of this one.

00:03:05.643 --> 00:03:08.062
All right guys, I'm Tony Gonzalez, and I'm here with Sleep Number.

00:03:08.271 --> 00:03:10.315
Sleep is something that I prioritize.

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:12.567
I think everything begins, before you even think about

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:15.987
nutrition or working out, you make sure you get a good night's sleep.

00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:20.366
It's totally underestimated, but it's something that can actually change your life, literally.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.326
Will make you happier,

00:03:21.326 --> 00:03:23.203
will help you make better decisions

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:27.540
and will fire you up. You might not even need that second, third cup of coffee,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.000
if you can get a good night's sleep.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.212
So make sure that you're out there getting your good rest.

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.088
And this is: Build Your Squad.

